sec.p:
All contents used in SMS, STS, and inpatient education were pre‐written and reviewed by HF specialists and senior nursing specialists (samples of SMS in Figure
1 ). The contents were based on HF diagnosis and management guidelines, review articles in UpToDate database, and educational materials from Heart Failure Society of America, including the following modules11, 12, 13, 14:
understanding HF;
HF symptoms, signs of exacerbation, and the right time to visit a doctor;
pharmacologic treatment of HF, including the purpose, necessity, and side effects of each medicine;
lifestyle modification, including smoking cessation, limiting salt and water intake, weighing, avoid catching cold, and regular exercise;
appointment adherence, including the appropriate time to visit a doctor, and the information a doctor needs to know; and
motivating and encouraging.
